# family: value
# bridge: A(law-restatement)
# regime: exact (the same rows over the same declarations, value for value)
# instrument-first: the GDScript suite this replaces, case for case
# baseline: tests/unit/wire, tests/integration/sync
# baseline-count: 115
# added-count: 9
#
# THE ADDED CASES are the shell-side proof of the lanes those slices wrote
# natively: `test_the_retained_row_heals_whole_then_masks_what_moved` in
# tests/unit/wire, and `test_a_retained_field_crosses_only_when_it_changes` and
# `test_the_input_lane_repeats_recent_ticks_rather_than_retransmitting` in
# tests/integration/sync. They were never in the baseline and license nothing,
# so they carry no row. `test_the_volatile_row_bails_on_a_missing_field` is the
# fourth, and it is a baseline case re-authored under a name that says what it
# now reads: its old name is dropped below rather than carried, because the
# frame it named is gone. The last five are the SYNC frame codec's laws restated
# on `NetwSyncKernel`, which now owns that layout outright.
#
# The declared property set's value plane: what a set's columns become on the
# wire, what a peer is owed of them, and what a receiver reconstructs. The
# family opens at Z1e, when Z1d's switch left the shell's masked send and its
# merge with no caller.
#
# WHY THE SCOPES ARE THESE TWO. `tests/unit/wire` is the codec and the books,
# `tests/integration/sync` is the same plane through a live pair. Scope
# permanence binds both to this family from here on, including the two stock
# conformance suites they contain: those are the argued permanent set (plan of
# record 9.1), and they read `CARRY kit` rather than leaving the scope.
#
# WHAT THE PORTED ROWS CLAIM. Each names the native law that now holds the
# thing the GDScript case held. They are not translations. The masked lane's
# decision moved from `NetwPropertySetBinding.masked_delta_for` to
# `netw::wire::BaselineBook` under `netw::repl::RowLane`, and its
# reconstruction from `NetwSyncKernel.decode_volatile`'s merge to
# `netw::repl::read_row_frame`. The native laws were written first and this
# ledger is the audit that nothing was lost when the shell halves went.
#
# WHAT STAYS. Everything reading `CARRY shell` is the shell codec that has not
# moved: the freshness books, the datagram magics, and the compat path over
# Channel.SYNC. Z2 dissolves those, and this ledger cannot close until it has.
#
# The three derived lanes have all left. The retained one went to
# Channel.SYNC_ROW_DELTA, where `netw::repl::RetainedLane` holds the diff and
# advances it on send rather than on an ack. The windowed input ring went to
# Channel.SYNC_ROW_WINDOW, where `netw::repl::WindowRing` holds the range in
# flight and `netw::repl::write_window_frame` carries it as ages below the
# frame tick.
